# Keep secrets and local state out of the build context.
#
# This file is load-bearing for security, not just build speed. The Dockerfile
# does `COPY . .` in the build stage; without these exclusions the production
# .env — database passwords, JWT secret, API keys — would be written into an
# image layer. Layers are not erased by a later delete: anyone who can pull the
# image can read it back. Env belongs at runtime via env_file, never at build.
#
# Patterns are ** so they match at ANY depth. Bare `.env` matches only the
# context root — a `config/.env` or `secrets/prod.pem` would have sailed
# straight into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Never ship a dump. These contain real customer conversations.
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.gz
**/backups/

# Rebuilt inside the image; copying the host's would defeat the point of a
# reproducible build (and Alpine cannot use Windows/glibc native binaries).
node_modules/
dist/

# Not needed at runtime.
.git/
.github/
test/
coverage/
*.spec.ts
*.e2e-spec.ts
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
docs/
ops/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
